problem:
### Example 5E, F, G (Workbook p. 49)
From the graph of $y = h(x)$:
- **E. $x$-intercept:** \underline{\hspace{2cm}}
- **F. $y$-intercept:** \underline{\hspace{2cm}}
- **G. Slope ($m$):** \underline{\hspace{2cm}}

solution:
$$\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{x\text{-intercept: }} & \mathbf{\left(\frac{4}{3}, 0\right) \approx (1.33, 0)} \quad (\text{where line crosses } x\text{-axis}) \\[0.5em]
\mathbf{y\text{-intercept: }} & \mathbf{(0, -2)} \quad (\text{where line crosses } y\text{-axis}) \\[0.5em]
\mathbf{\text{Slope } m: } & \text{From } (0, -2) \text{ to } (2, 1): \\
& m = \frac{1 - (-2)}{2 - 0} = \mathbf{\frac{3}{2} = 1.5}
\end{aligned}$$
